.SH Bar state style
.PP
When \fBbar\-css\-states\fR is enabled, the following classes are added to
\fBwindow#waybar\fR:
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fBwindow#waybar.\&toplevel\-active\fR
.IP \(bu 4
\fBwindow#waybar.\&toplevel\-maximized\fR
.IP \(bu 4
\fBwindow#waybar.\&toplevel\-minimized\fR
.IP \(bu 4
\fBwindow#waybar.\&toplevel\-fullscreen\fR
.PD
.PP
The active, minimized classes describe the active application.\& The maximized
and fullscreen classes are set if any non\-minimized application known to belong
to the active workspace has that state.\&
.PP
Workspace membership is learned when an application is activated and requires
the compositor to support \fBext\-workspace\-v1\fR.\& Before an application has been
activated during the current Waybar session, its workspace may be unknown.\& On
compositors without \fBext\-workspace\-v1\fR, these classes fall back to the active
application'\&s state.\&
.PP
For example:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
window#waybar {
	background\-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0\&.5);
}

window#waybar\&.toplevel\-maximized {
	background\-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1);
}
.fi
.RE
